From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Fall back to ComputerName when ActiveComputerName
 is missing.

GetComputerNameExW reads the NetBIOS name from the volatile
ActiveComputerName key, which only wineboot creates. A prefix that runs
without wineboot (on PS5 a title cannot start it) has only the stored
ComputerName\ComputerName key, so GetComputerNameW failed with
ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. dxdiagn's IDxDiagProvider::Initialize then
returned E_FAIL, and GUN stopped at its DirectX check.

When ActiveComputerName cannot be opened, read the NetBIOS name from
ComputerName\ComputerName, the key wineboot copies it from.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/registry.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/registry.c b/dlls/kernelbase/registry.c
index 7ec30c2..3a77f27 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/registry.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/registry.c
@@ -3360,7 +3360,12 @@ BOOL WINAPI GetComputerNameExW( COMPUTER_NAME_FORMAT type, WCHAR *name, DWORD *l
         return FALSE;
     }
 
-    if (!(ret = RegOpenKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, keyname, 0, KEY_READ, &key )))
+    ret = RegOpenKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, keyname, 0, KEY_READ, &key );
+    /* ActiveComputerName is volatile and only wineboot creates it. */
+    if (ret && (type == ComputerNameNetBIOS || type == ComputerNamePhysicalNetBIOS))
+        ret = RegOpenKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, L"System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\ComputerName\\ComputerName",
+                             0, KEY_READ, &key );
+    if (!ret)
     {
         DWORD size = *len * sizeof(WCHAR);
         ret = RegQueryValueExW( key, valuename, NULL, NULL, (BYTE *)name, &size );
